loudly|high-volume-manner|ADVERB|At a high volume|In a way that produces a lot of sound or at a high volume.|một cách lớn tiếng|The children cheered loudly when the parade reached the square.|Lũ trẻ reo hò thật lớn khi đoàn diễu hành đến quảng trường.|An adverb that modifies an action or another phrase; formed from loud with -ly.|loudly
origin|beginning-or-source|NOUN|Beginning or source|The point or source from which something begins or is derived.|nguồn gốc; xuất xứ|The guide explained the origin of the festival.|Hướng dẫn viên giải thích nguồn gốc của lễ hội.|Countable noun; commonly followed by of, as in the origin of a custom.|origin
fool|person-who-acts-unwisely|NOUN|Person considered foolish|A person thought to behave or speak foolishly, especially by showing little intelligence.|kẻ ngốc; người bị cho là thiếu khôn ngoan|The fool forgot to check which platform the train used.|Kẻ ngốc ấy đã quên kiểm tra chuyến tàu khởi hành ở sân ga nào.|Countable noun; a fool, plural fools. The available Vocab4600 definition is truncated, so this wording stays with the visible idea and Vietnamese gloss.|fool
battery|electricity-supplying-cell|NOUN|Electricity-supplying object|A source of electrical power used to operate a device.|pin; ắc quy|The flashlight stopped working because its battery was empty.|Đèn pin ngừng sáng vì pin đã cạn.|Countable noun; a battery for a device, or the battery in a device.|battery
boxed|inside-a-package|ADJECTIVE|Inside a box or package|Contained in a box or package.|được đóng hộp|A boxed set of pencils sat beside the open sketchbook.|Một bộ bút chì được đóng hộp nằm cạnh cuốn sổ phác thảo đang mở.|Adjective describing something placed in a box or package; it can appear before a noun.|boxed
collide|hit-while-moving|VERB|Hit while moving|To hit another moving person or thing with force.|va chạm với; đụng vào|The carts collided in the narrow hallway.|Những chiếc xe đẩy va vào nhau trong hành lang hẹp.|Usually intransitive; collide with names the other person or thing.|collide
birthplace|birth-or-origin-place|NOUN|Place of birth or beginning|The place a person is born, or the starting point of something.|nơi sinh; nơi khởi nguồn|The biography names a small town as the painter's birthplace.|Cuốn tiểu sử ghi tên một thị trấn nhỏ là nơi sinh của họa sĩ.|Countable noun; birthplace of a person or of something that began in a place.|birthplace
posture|body-position|NOUN|Position of the body|The way a person holds their body while standing or sitting.|tư thế; tư thế đứng hoặc ngồi|Lina adjusted her posture before sitting at the desk.|Lina điều chỉnh tư thế trước khi ngồi vào bàn.|Usually uncountable for the way someone holds their body; improve or adjust your posture.|posture
responsible|accountable-or-in-charge|ADJECTIVE|Having a duty or authority|Having the duty or authority to deal with a task, person, or organization.|chịu trách nhiệm; có trách nhiệm với một việc|Mina is responsible for checking that the studio door is locked.|Mina chịu trách nhiệm kiểm tra xem cửa phòng thu đã khóa chưa.|Adjective; responsible for a task or for doing something.|responsible
responsible|dependable-character|ADJECTIVE|Conscientious in conduct|Having a sense of duty and behaving conscientiously.|có trách nhiệm; chu đáo trong cách cư xử|The team chose a responsible volunteer to keep track of the shared supplies.|Nhóm chọn một tình nguyện viên có trách nhiệm để theo dõi đồ dùng chung.|Adjective used before a person or after be; keep this character description distinct from being responsible for a specified task.|responsible
maintenance|care-or-repair|NOUN|Care or repair to keep something working|The work of keeping a building or system in good condition through regular care or repair.|việc bảo trì; sự bảo dưỡng|The school scheduled elevator maintenance during the break.|Trường lên lịch bảo trì thang máy trong kỳ nghỉ.|Usually uncountable; maintenance of a building, system, or equipment.|maintenance
maintenance|preserving-a-state|NOUN|Keeping a situation continuing|The act of keeping a condition or situation continuing.|sự duy trì; việc giữ cho một tình trạng tiếp diễn|The maintenance of calm between the teams depended on clear rules.|Việc duy trì sự bình tĩnh giữa hai đội phụ thuộc vào các quy tắc rõ ràng.|Usually followed by of; this abstract use is distinct from repair work.|maintenance
bow|lower-body-as-respect|VERB|Lower the head or upper body|To lower the head or upper body forwards as a sign of respect or greeting.|cúi đầu; cúi chào|When the host welcomed her, she bowed slightly.|Khi chủ nhà chào đón, cô khẽ cúi chào.|Intransitive verb; bow to a person or group. Past tense and past participle: bowed.|bow
bow|weapon-for-arrows|NOUN|Weapon for shooting arrows|A curved weapon made with a string and used to shoot arrows.|cây cung; cung tên|The museum displayed a wooden bow beside several arrows.|Bảo tàng trưng bày một cây cung bằng gỗ bên cạnh vài mũi tên.|Countable noun; often used with arrow, as in a bow and arrow.|bow
bow|act-of-bowing|NOUN|Act of bowing|An act of lowering the head or upper body as a greeting or sign of respect.|cái cúi chào|Her bow was brief, and she then left the stage.|Cái cúi chào của cô diễn ra ngắn gọn, rồi cô rời sân khấu.|Countable noun; take or make a bow.|bow
bow|decorative-loop|NOUN|Decorative ribbon loop|A decorative knot or loop made by tying ribbon or similar material.|nơ; chiếc nơ trang trí|A small blue bow held the ribbon around the parcel.|Một chiếc nơ xanh nhỏ giữ dải ruy băng quanh gói hàng.|Countable noun; a bow on or in something; plural bows.|bow
bow|front-of-a-ship|NOUN|Forward end of a ship|The forward end of a ship.|mũi tàu|A rope was secured near the bow of the boat.|Một sợi dây được buộc gần mũi thuyền.|Countable noun; commonly the bow of a ship or boat.|bow
bow|string-instrument-playing-stick|NOUN|Stick for playing a string instrument|A stick with strings or hair that is moved across the strings of a violin or another string instrument to make sound.|vĩ kéo của đàn violin hoặc nhạc cụ dây|The violinist lifted the bow from its case before rehearsal.|Nghệ sĩ violin lấy cây vĩ ra khỏi hộp trước buổi tập.|Countable noun; draw or move a bow across the strings of an instrument.|bow
deter|discourage-or-prevent|VERB|Discourage or prevent an action|To make someone less willing to do something or to prevent an action.|ngăn cản; làm nản lòng|The long queue did not deter Amira from joining the tour.|Hàng người xếp dài không làm Amira nản lòng, cô vẫn tham gia chuyến tham quan.|Transitive verb; deter someone from doing something.|deter
talk|speak-to-express-thoughts|VERB|Speak to express thoughts|To say words to another person to express thoughts or exchange information.|nói chuyện; trao đổi suy nghĩ|We talked quietly about our plans on the walk home.|Trên đường đi bộ về nhà, chúng tôi trò chuyện nhỏ nhẹ về các dự định.|Usually intransitive; talk to or with someone, or talk about a subject.|talk
talk|spoken-conversation|NOUN|Spoken conversation|An occasion when people speak with one another.|cuộc trò chuyện|After the walk, they had a short talk about the route.|Sau buổi đi bộ, họ có một cuộc trò chuyện ngắn về lộ trình.|Countable noun; have a talk with someone or about a subject. The source provides a Vietnamese gloss but no English example for this reading.|talk
talk|spoken-presentation|NOUN|Spoken presentation|A speech or presentation given to an audience about a subject.|bài nói chuyện; bài thuyết trình|After lunch, the engineer gave a talk about bridge design.|Sau bữa trưa, kỹ sư trình bày một bài nói chuyện về thiết kế cầu.|Countable noun; give a talk about or on a subject.|talk
aroma|pleasant-or-notable-smell|NOUN|Noticeable scent|A noticeable smell or scent, often from food or drink.|hương thơm; mùi hương|An aroma of toasted bread drifted from the kitchen.|Hương thơm của bánh mì nướng lan ra từ nhà bếp.|Countable or uncountable noun; aroma of something names the source of a scent.|aroma
experimental|tested-using-new-methods|ADJECTIVE|Based on methods being tested|Based on new ideas, forms, or methods tried in order to discover their effects.|mang tính thử nghiệm|The team used an experimental method to test a new water filter.|Nhóm dùng một phương pháp thử nghiệm để kiểm tra bộ lọc nước mới.|Adjective; commonly used before a noun such as method, treatment, or work.|experimental
exclusively|only-for-a-particular-use|ADVERB|Only for a particular use|Only for one particular person, group, or purpose.|chỉ; dành riêng cho|The meeting room was reserved exclusively for the evening class.|Phòng họp được dành riêng cho lớp học buổi tối.|Adverb modifying a verb or phrase; exclusively to a group or exclusively for a purpose.|exclusively
attachment|email-file|NOUN|File sent with a message|A file included with an email or another digital message.|tệp đính kèm|Please save the spreadsheet attachment before closing the message.|Vui lòng lưu tệp bảng tính đính kèm trước khi đóng thư.|Countable noun; an attachment to an email or message.|attachment
attachment|emotional-bond|NOUN|Emotional bond|A strong feeling of affection or connection to a person or place.|sự gắn bó; tình cảm gắn bó|Even after moving away, Bao felt a deep attachment to his neighborhood.|Dù đã chuyển đi, Bảo vẫn cảm thấy gắn bó sâu sắc với khu phố của mình.|Usually followed by to when naming the person or place connected to.|attachment
attachment|act-of-joining|NOUN|Act of joining|The act of joining or fixing one thing to another.|sự gắn; việc gắn một vật vào vật khác|The attachment of the sensor to the frame took only a minute.|Việc gắn cảm biến vào khung chỉ mất một phút.|Often followed by of the thing attached and to the thing receiving it.|attachment
attachment|joining-object|NOUN|Object that joins things|A thing that joins or can be attached to another thing.|vật nối; bộ phận gắn thêm|A metal attachment connects the handle to the cabinet door.|Một bộ phận kim loại nối tay nắm với cánh tủ.|Countable noun; an attachment for or to a larger object. The available definition supports this reading, though its source example does not illustrate it.|attachment
necessity|needed-thing|NOUN|Something needed|Something that is needed or essential.|điều cần thiết; vật thiết yếu|Clean drinking water is a necessity during the long trip.|Nước uống sạch là thứ thiết yếu trong chuyến đi dài.|Countable noun; a necessity for someone or something; plural necessities.|necessity
necessity|fact-of-being-needed|NOUN|Fact that something is needed|The state or fact that something is needed.|sự cần thiết; tính cần thiết|They questioned the necessity of replacing the working chairs.|Họ đặt câu hỏi về sự cần thiết của việc thay những chiếc ghế vẫn dùng tốt.|Abstract noun; commonly followed by of plus a noun or gerund.|necessity
emotionally|connected-with-feelings|ADVERB|In a way connected with feelings|In a manner related to a person's emotional state.|về mặt cảm xúc|The speech affected the audience emotionally.|Bài phát biểu tác động đến khán giả về mặt cảm xúc.|Adverb modifying a verb or adjective; emotionally connected or affected.|emotionally
emotionally|showing-strong-feeling|ADVERB|Showing strong feeling|In a way that shows or expresses strong feelings.|một cách xúc động; thể hiện cảm xúc|He answered emotionally while describing the farewell.|Anh trả lời đầy xúc động khi kể về buổi chia tay.|Adverb describing how someone speaks or responds. This expressive reading is based on a Vietnamese gloss and has no independent English definition in the source.|emotionally
apparatus|purpose-built-equipment|NOUN|Equipment for a purpose|Equipment or a device designed for a particular purpose.|thiết bị; dụng cụ|Technicians installed the apparatus before measuring the air pressure.|Các kỹ thuật viên lắp đặt thiết bị trước khi đo áp suất không khí.|Often followed by for plus a purpose; apparatus can refer to equipment used together.|apparatus
apparatus|organized-institutional-system|NOUN|Organized institutional system|The organized parts and structure of an institution or organization.|bộ máy; hệ thống tổ chức|The agency reorganized its administrative apparatus last year.|Cơ quan đã tổ chức lại bộ máy hành chính vào năm ngoái.|Often used before a noun such as administrative or in the phrase apparatus of an institution; keep distinct from equipment.|apparatus
